algorithms.pseudocode:
VARIABLE-ELIMINATION(f, domains[1..k]):
  // Theorem: min_{x1,...,xk} f = min_{x1} min_{x2} ... min_{xk} f
  best ← +∞
  for x1 in domains[1]:
    for x2 in domains[2]:
      ...
        for xk in domains[k]:
          best ← min(best, f(x1,...,xk))
  return best

Time: O(∏|domains[i]|)
For factorized costs: exploits independence for exponential speedup
